									</description></item><item><title>Nintendo’s Switch 2 console is $50 off for Black Friday</title><link>https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/1038181/nintendo-switch-2-black-friday-deal-mario-kart-world-bundle-2026-sale</link><guid>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1038181</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0500</pubDate><description>
											

						
&lt;figure&gt;

&lt;img alt="A photo of the Nintendo Switch 2 running Mario Kart World in handheld mode." data-caption="" data-portal-copyright="Photo: Amelia Holowaty Krales / The Verge" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/06/257769_Switch_2_AKrales_0093_fe9169.jpg?quality=90&amp;#038;strip=all&amp;#038;crop=0,0,100,100" /&gt;
	&lt;figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Those hoping to save some cash on a &lt;strong&gt;Nintendo Switch 2&lt;/strong&gt; can do so starting today, November 22nd, through Saturday, December 5th, giving you plenty of time to think about it after Cyber Monday has passed. For a limited time, Nintendo has knocked $50 off one of its two current console bundles, temporarily rolling back the &lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/1027757/nintendo-switch-2-price-hike-plans-ram" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;$50 price increase&lt;/a&gt; that went into effect in early September.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;It’s tough to predict which bundle will be most popular for your household. The &lt;em&gt;Mario Kart World&lt;/em&gt; bundle runs $499.99 (previously $549.99) and includes the console, a digital copy of the aforementioned game, and three months of Nintendo Switch Online. Then there’s the &lt;em&gt;Nintendo Switch Sports Resort&lt;/em&gt; bundle for $529.99 (price unchanged for Black Friday), which includes the more recent minigame-filled title instead. Both are currently available from &lt;a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HGHB3V16"&gt;Amazon&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://www.bestbuy.com/product/switch-2-mario-kart-world-bundle/J7GSL57WWG/sku/6689812"&gt;Best Buy&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://www.walmart.com/ip/Nintendo-Switch-2-Mario-Kart-World-Bundle/20865751029"&gt;Walmart&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href="https://www.nintendo.com/us/store/products/nintendo-switch-2-mario-kart-world-bundle-128067/"&gt;Nintendo&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="product-block"&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Nintendo Switch 2 + Mario Kart World Bundle&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;figure class="product-image"&gt;&lt;img loading="lazy" width="300" height="200" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Nintendo-Switch-2-Mario-Kart-World-Bundle-Box-Art.jpg?w=300" class="attachment-medium size-medium" alt="" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Where to Buy:&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HGHB3V16"&gt; &lt;strike&gt;$549.99&lt;/strike&gt; $499.99 at &lt;strong&gt;Amazon&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.walmart.com/ip/Nintendo-Switch-2-Mario-Kart-World-Bundle/20865751029"&gt; &lt;strike&gt;$549.99&lt;/strike&gt; $499 at &lt;strong&gt;Walmart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.bestbuy.com/product/switch-2-mario-kart-world-bundle/J7GSL57WWG/sku/6689812"&gt; &lt;strike&gt;$549.99&lt;/strike&gt; $499.99 at &lt;strong&gt;Best Buy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Nintendo has delivered hit after hit since the console launched in mid-2025. There are now plenty of excellent games to justify snagging a Switch 2, including, most recently, the &lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/1025415/the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time-review-nintendo-switch-2"&gt;stellar remake of &lt;em&gt;The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Plus, the newer console can play nearly all of the original Switch games, and it’s wirelessly compatible with the older system’s Joy-Con and Switch Pro controllers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;If you’re planning to get a Switch 2, below are some useful guides filled with accessory recommendations. From tempered glass screen protectors and protective cases to controllers, there are plenty of goodies that’ll help you take better care of your Switch 2 and get more enjoyment from it.&lt;/p&gt;
						
									</description></item><item><title>‘The show is starting soon. Please turn on your headphones.’</title><link>https://www.theverge.com/tech/1038879/off-broadway-love-me-auracast</link><guid>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1038879</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0500</pubDate><description>
											

						
&lt;figure&gt;

&lt;img alt="Drew Michael on stage in the off-Broadway show Love Me." data-caption="Love Me uses Auracast broadcasts both for accessibility and the sound design. | Photo: Curtis Brown" data-portal-copyright="Photo: Curtis Brown" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/love-me-off-broadway-auracast-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;#038;strip=all&amp;#038;crop=0,0,100,100" /&gt;
	&lt;figcaption&gt;
	Love Me uses Auracast broadcasts both for accessibility and the sound design. | Photo: Curtis Brown	&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Up a few concrete steps and through the front door of a 200-year-old row house in New York City, I follow a crowd of people into the 178-seat SoHo Playhouse. As we filter to our seats, ushers hand each person a black drawstring bag with a pair of wired headphones connected to &lt;a href="https://www.auriaudio.com/products/auri-rx1-receiver/"&gt;a small Auracast receiver&lt;/a&gt;. Then, soon after the play begins, we're instructed to put them on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;The headphones are an integral storytelling tool of &lt;a href="https://www.sohoplayhouse.com/shows/drew-michael-love-me"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Love Me&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; - a one-man show from the minds of stand-up comedian and former &lt;em&gt;Saturday Night Live&lt;/em&gt; writer Drew Michael and director Prashanth Venkataramanujam. It's a show about love and the bid for connection, told in five chapters …&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1038879/off-broadway-love-me-auracast"&gt;Read the full story at The Verge.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
						
									</description></item><item><title>How Tamagotchis got us hooked on digital pets</title><link>https://www.theverge.com/podcast/1039716/tamagotchi-history-digital-pets-anniversary</link><guid>https://www.theverge.com/?p=1039716</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:15:27 -0500</pubDate><description>
											

						
&lt;figure&gt;

&lt;img alt="" data-caption="" data-portal-copyright="" data-has-syndication-rights="1" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/VRH_Tamagotchi_Site.jpg?quality=90&amp;#038;strip=all&amp;#038;crop=0,0,100,100" /&gt;
	&lt;figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/figcaption&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;If you were are a kid in the late 1990s, there's a near-100 percent chance you either had a Tamagotchi or knew someone who did. The tiny digital pets came out of nowhere and became an overnight sensation, as millions of kids signed up to parent a crying, hungry, constantly dirty creature. Until they went to school, anyway, at which point their parents were given some new responsibilities they neither asked for nor wanted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;On this episode of &lt;em&gt;Version History, &lt;/em&gt;we dig deep into the story of the Tamagotchi. That story has its 30th anniversary this week, even though the real craze only lasted a few years. David Pierce is joined by &lt;em&gt;The Verge's &lt;/em&gt;Mia …&lt;/p&gt;
